FAQ = [{'q': 'What travel documents do I need to bring?', 'a': "Non-U.S. Citizens - click\xa0 here \n Canadian Citizens - click\xa0 here \n U.S. Permanent Residents - click\xa0 here \n U.S. Citizens\xa0 \n Proper travel documentation is required at embarkation and throughout the cruise. Even though a guest has completed registration using Online Check-in, it is still the responsibility of the guest to present the required travel documents at the time of embarkation. Guests should check with their travel agent and/or government authority to determine the travel documents necessary for each port of call. Any guest without proper documents will not be allowed to board the vessel and no refund of the cruise fare will be issued. Carnival assumes no responsibility for advising guests of proper travel documentation. \n Except where it is a mandatory requirement, Carnival highly recommends that all guests travel with a passport book.\xa0 The passport book must be valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel. This will enhance the debarkation experience as delays may be expected upon return to the United States for those without one. Additionally, this will enable guests to fly from the United States to meet their ship at a foreign port should they miss their scheduled port of embarkation and allow guests who must disembark the ship before their cruise ends, due to an emergency, to fly back to the United States without significant delays and complications. \n U.S. Domestic Cruises \n For certain cruises that begin and end in the same U.S port, the following WHTI-compliant documents are acceptable for cruise travel (please see below for travel document requirements for voyages visiting Colombia, Greenland, Martinique and Panama ). \xa0* \n U.S. Passport Book (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel) \n U.S. Passport Card (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel) \n State Enhanced Driver's License \n Certificate of U.S. Naturalization \n Native American Indian Card \n U.S.-born citizens may also use a birth certificate (issued by a government agency or Department of Health and Vital Statistics) and accompanied by government-issued photo ID; a Mobile/Digital version of a photo ID is not an acceptable form of identification. \n * Travel document exceptions for U.S. domestic cruises that begin and end in the same U.S. homeport, calling on the following ports of call: \n Colombia - mandatory requirement for passport book or card (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel).\n Greenland - mandatory requirement for passport book (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel).\n Panama - passport book (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel) required for guests who wish to go ashore in Panama. Guests using another form of WHTI-compliant document (including a passport card) to sail must remain on board when the ship visits Panama.\n Martinique, FWI -\xa0 passport book (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel) required for guests who wish to go ashore in Martinique. Guests using another form of WHTI-compliant document (including a passport card) to sail\xa0 must \xa0remain on board when the ship visits Martinique. \n * \xa0Travel document exceptions for U.S. domestic cruises that begin and end in different\xa0 U.S. homeports: \xa0 Mandatory requirement for \xa0passport book or passport card (valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel).\n Australia, New Zealand, Asia and Transpacific Cruises \n U.S citizens are required to carry a passport book, valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel.\xa0Visas and/or specific travel documentation may be required for some destinations.\n Europe and Transatlantic Cruises \n U.S citizens are required to carry a passport book, valid for at least six months beyond the completion of travel.\n ETA – UK Electronic Travel Authorization \n All travelers (as of January 8, 2025) who do not hold a passport to the United Kingdom or Ireland must obtain an electronic visa, know"}, {'q': 'What do I need to do to get on board?', 'a': "All guests must complete their Online Check-in process no later than midnight (Eastern time) prior to their sailing date. During online check-in, you will be asked to select an arrival appointment. This is the time that everyone in your stateroom should be at the cruise port terminal.\nPlease arrive promptly within your Arrival Appointment\xa0to reduce your wait time in line.\nAt check-in, you must present your boarding pass, picture ID and citizenship documents (including any necessary visas).\xa0 Due to security protocol, last minute bookings made within 24 hours of sailing will require guests to undergo a secondary screening.\xa0\n Guests who are scheduled to arrive at the terminal before 1:30 PM, usually check their bags with a porter so they can be free to enjoy lunch on Lido Deck before access to their stateroom is granted.\nChecked baggage service is only available until 2 hours before the ship's published departure time.\xa0Guests arriving after this time will be responsible for taking their bags on board.\xa0 \nLunch is served on Lido Deck from boarding until the commencement of the safety briefing.\n Final Boarding :\xa0\xa0In preparation for departure, all guests must be on board by the Final Boarding time printed on your boarding pass or you will not be permitted to sail."}, {'q': "What is Carnival's Liquor & Beverage Policy?", 'a': "The policy below is for cruise departures from the U.S.; for cruises sailing from Australia, click here .\xa0 \n Drinking Alcohol On Board \n The minimum age for the purchase and/or consumption of\nalcoholic beverages in the bars, lounges and gift shops is 21 years of age.\nCarnival reserves the right to request ID prior to the purchase of alcohol and\nrefuse the sale of alcohol to anyone.\xa0 \n Bringing Liquor and Beverages On Board - Embarkation \n Guests are prohibited from bringing water, sodas and other\nnon-alcoholic beverages that are packaged in glass or plastic bottles. \n On embarkation day, a small quantity of non-alcoholic\nbeverages (i.e., sparkling water, sodas, energy drinks, juice, and milk),\npackaged in cans or cartons, may be brought on board and must be in the guest's\ncarry-on luggage. A small quantity is considered a maximum of 12 sealed,\nunopened cans/cartons of 12-ounces/354-ml each or less, per person. \n Guests are prohibited from bringing alcoholic beverages on\nboard with the following exception - at the beginning of the cruise during\nembarkation day only, guests (21 years of age and older) may bring one 750-ml\nbottle of sealed/unopened wine or champagne, per person, in their carry-on\nluggage.* Outside this exception, all liquor, beer, other forms of alcoholic and\nnon-alcoholic beverages are strictly prohibited in both carry-on and checked\nluggage and such items will be confiscated and discarded and no compensation\nwill be provided. Guests sailing with us on back-to-back cruises are entitled\nto bring the same quantity as stated in this policy, per cruise. The additional\nquantities will be stored for safekeeping at the start of the first cruise and\nwill be given to the guest as each following cruise begins. \n * Port, Vermouth, Sherry and other fortified wines, over 15% alcohol by volume (ABV), cannot be brought on board.\xa0 \n Corkage Fee \n Should guests wish to consume their wine or champagne in the\nmain dining room, specialty restaurant or bar, a $15.00 USD corkage fee, per\n750-ml bottle, will be charged. A corkage fee is a charge that is assessed, at\ntime of service, for every bottle that is served and not bought on the\npremises. \n Bottled Water \n For convenience, guests can purchase bottled water prior to\nthe cruise and it will be delivered to the stateroom on embarkation day.\nBottled water may also be purchased on board by contacting room service. Once\non board, the purchase is non-refundable and guests may take home any unopened\nbottles. \n To ensure we have an ample supply, please visit The Fun\nShops™ at\xa0 www.carnival.com/funshops \xa0to place your order before your cruise. \n $19.20 USD (includes 20% delivery\nfee) for a 12-pack of bottled water (16.9-ounce bottle/500-ml bottle) \n $5.40 USD (includes 20% delivery\nfee) for 1 large, bottled water (50.72-ounce bottle/1.5-liter bottle) \n $29.94 USD (includes 20% delivery\nfee) for 8-pack of bottled water (50.72-ounce bottle/1.5-liter bottle)\xa0 \n Distilled Water for CPAP Machines \n Carnival carries distilled water for CPAP machines which can be purchased\neither pre-cruise or once on board. Guests can purchase pre-cruise online at www.carnival.com/in-room-food-beverages or by contacting \xa0our Fun\nShops department at 800-522-7648,\xa0Monday through Friday, 9:00am-10:00pm ET and Saturday and Sunday, 9:00am-6:00pm ET. \xa0For purchase on board, please contact room service. Should\nyou wish to bring your own distilled water with you, it must be hand carried\nalong with your CPAP machine. \n Coolers \n Guests are prohibited from bringing large coolers since\nscreening and movement of large coolers through embarkation is an impediment to\nthe boarding and security process. However, for the purpose of carrying small\nquantities of non-alcoholic beverages and/or medications small, personal-sized\ncoolers, no larger than 12” x 12” x 12” are permitted as carry-on luggage. \n Purchasing Liquor Pre-Cruise through The Fun Shops \n All products sold containing alcohol have a limit of two products per statero"}, {'q': 'What are the CHEERS! and CHEERS! Zero Proof Beverage Programs?', 'a': "What is the CHEERS! Beverage Program? \n CHEERS! is an all-inclusive beverage program that allows guests to enjoy a wide range of alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages by paying a flat daily rate. Guests must be 21 or older to purchase CHEERS! and each adult assigned to the same stateroom must purchase the program. \n Our CHEERS! beverage program includes a great variety of non-alcoholic beverages, as well as a wide selection of high quality brand-name spirits and wines by the glass. \n How to Purchase CHEERS!: \n Before your cruise: \xa0CHEERS! can be purchased at\xa0 www.carnival.com/funshops \xa0or by contacting The Fun Shops department at 800-522-7648, Monday through Friday, 9:00am-10:00pm ET and Saturday and Sunday, 9:00am-6:00pm ET. Cut-off for pre-purchase online is 11:59pm ET, the evening prior to the cruise departure. Although we are not able to process the Carnival Gift Card for Fun Shop orders by telephone, you may use a Carnival Gift Card when purchasing CHEERS! online. \n $83.94 USD per person, per day including 20% service charge \n On board your cruise: \xa0 Once on board your cruise, CHEERS! can be purchased at bar locations. \n $89.94 USD per person, per day including 20% service charge \nAustralia and Eastbound Transpacific Cruises: For pricing and age restrictions, CHEERS! can be purchased online at www.carnival.com.au/drink-packages or by contacting our Australia Desk, Monday through Sunday, 7:00am-6:00pm AEST, at 1 300 385 625 (from Australia) and 0800 442 095 (from New Zealand).\xa0 If you are calling from the U.S. or Canada, please contact 'The Fun Shops' Department at 800 522-7648, Monday through Friday, 9:00am-10:00pm ET and Saturday and Sunday, 9:00am-6:00pm ET.\n Included in the price of your cruise, served in the main dining room and available 24/7 in the Lido Restaurant: non-bottled water, lemonade, unsweetened iced tea, hot chocolate and non-specialty coffee and tea. \n To view a sample of beverages prices for individual drinks and CHEERS! Q&A's, click here . \n CHEERS! Includes: \n All spirits, including cocktails, cognacs, whiskies and other spirits, as well as beer (including self-serve beer stations - PYOB) and wine and champagne by the glass, with a $20.00 USD or lower menu price, per serving \n Sodas (including specialty sodas), zero-proof frozen cocktails (including smoothies) and juices \n Specialty coffees and hot tea served in the main dining rooms, specialty restaurants and coffee bars \n Milkshakes, where available \n Energy drinks \n 500-ml bottled water and other non-alcoholic bottled beverages served in bars and lounges \n Packaged water in the dining rooms and specialty restaurants \n 25% discount off the menu price for any spirit, cocktail or wine by the glass, costing above $20.00 USD, per serving \n 25% discount off the menu price for wine and champagne by the bottle \n 25% discount off beverage seminars and classes \n CHEERS! Excludes: \n Beverages promoted and sold in souvenir glasses \n Bottles of liquor \n Beverages offered at the gangway \n Beverages offered through room service and/or other in-stateroom beverage programs \n Beverages purchased off the ship at any port of call, including Celebration Key, Half Moon Cay and Princess Cays \n Sharing cocktails, floaters, pitchers, tubes and buckets \n Beverages offered through enomatic wine machines \n Freshly squeezed orange juice served in the Havana Bar \n Main Dining Room freshly squeezed juice\xa0 \n All other beverage-related programs including merchandise, cigars and cigarettes \n Food items \n CHEERS! Program Restrictions: \n Guests must be 21 years or older to purchase and agree not to give to minors \n Each adult assigned to the same stateroom must purchase the program \n CHEERS! is non-transferable \n Guests must purchase the program for the entire cruise; this program is not offered on a per day basis \n If the program is purchased prior to the cruise, it is refundable up to 10:00pm ET, the evening prior to the cruise departure.\xa0 Otherwise, CHEERS! is non-refundable \n Pri"}, {'q': 'Is there a beverage package for soft drinks?', 'a': "Sail refreshed with Carnival's Bottomless Bubbles™ unlimited soda program! Enjoy the ease and convenience of paying one flat price for thirst-quenching fountain soda and juice all cruise long!\n Pre-Cruise and Onboard Prices:\xa0 \n Kids (17 years of age and younger): $8.34 USD\xa0per person, per day including 20% service charge \n Adults (18 years of age and older): $14.38 USD\xa0per person, per day including 20% service charge\xa0 \n Bottomless Bubbles can be purchased online at\xa0 www.carnival.com/funshops \xa0or by contacting The Fun Shops™ Department at 800 522-7648, Monday through Friday, 9:00am-10:00pm ET and Saturday and Sunday, 9:00am-6:00pm ET. Cut-off for pre-purchase online is at 11:59pm ET, the evening prior to the cruise departure. Bottomless Bubbles can also be purchased on board at bar locations. \nAustralia and Eastbound Transpacific Cruises: For pricing and age restrictions, CHEERS! can be purchased online at www.carnival.com.au/drink-packages or by contacting our Australia Desk, Monday through Sunday, 7:00am-6:00pm AEST, at 1 300 385 625 (from Australia) and 0800 442 095 (from New Zealand).\xa0 If you are calling from the U.S. or Canada, please contact 'The Fun Shops' Department at 800 522-7648, Monday through Friday, 9:00am-10:00pm ET and Saturday and Sunday, 9:00am-6:00pm ET.\n Currently, we are not able to process the Carnival Gift Card for Fun Shop orders by telephone. If you wish to purchase Bottomless Bubbles with a Carnival Gift Card, you may do so online at www.carnival.com/funshops \n Upon purchasing Bottomless Bubbles, a sticker will be placed on the guest's Sail & Sign® card. In all areas where beverage service is offered, guests may show the Bottomless Bubbles sticker and receive a glass of the carbonated soft drink of their choice. Juices may also be requested. One 16-ounce glass will be served at a time (10-ounce glass for juice) and only to the guest whose name appears on the Sail & Sign card with the Bottomless Bubbles sticker attached.\n The following beverages are offered through Bottomless Bubbles ( flavors may vary ):\n Soft Drinks/Soda \n Juices: Orange Juice, Cranberry Juice, Tomato Juice, Pineapple Juice and Grapefruit Juice \n Bottomless Bubbles excludes: \n Non-alcoholic beverages other than soda and juices listed above \n Beverages promoted and sold in souvenir glasses \n Bottled water \n Specialty coffee \n Beverages offered at gangway while debarking \n Beverages offered through room service or the interactive TV system (where applicable) or other in-stateroom beverage programs \n Please note: The following beverages are included in the price of your cruise and are served in the main dining room and 24/7 in the Lido Restaurant: non-bottled water, lemonade, iced tea and non-specialty coffee and tea. The following beverages are available through Room Service (charges may apply after 10:00am): juices (orange, tomato, apple or grapefruit), regular or decaffeinated coffee, hot tea, hot chocolate, chocolate milk, 2% milk and skim milk.\n The following restrictions apply: \n Price adjustments (up or down) implemented on the day of sailing will replace any previously advertised price. \n Only one beverage serving, per sticker, will be served at a time. There is a 10-minute wait between ordering drinks. \n Soft drink is served by the glass (16 ounces); juice is served by the glass (10 ounces). \n No sharing is permitted and is non-transferable. Guests or family members who would like to enjoy soft drinks through this program must purchase their own sticker. \n If Bottomless Bubbles is purchased prior to the cruise, it is refundable up to 10:00pm ET, the evening prior to the cruise departure. Otherwise, Bottomless Bubbles is non-refundable.\xa0 \n Program is only applicable for onboard purchases; program cannot be used for beverage purchases at Celebration Key, Half Moon Cay and Princess Cays in The Bahamas. \n Applicable state and local sales taxes will be charged to the guest's folio when this program is used within US waters. The tax i"}, {'q': 'What are my dining options?', 'a': "Guests may choose from\xa0three different dinner seating options. By popular request, all dining rooms are smoke-free. \n Assigned Seating - Early and Late Dining \n This dining option offers guests a pre-set dining time for the duration of the cruise as well as the same table assignment each evening in the Main Dining Room. Guests who choose this option will not be able to reserve 'Your Time' open seating once on board.\xa0\xa0 E arly dining may be scheduled between 5:30pm and 6:00pm and late dining , between 7:45pm and 8:15pm. * \n To give guests greater flexibility, assigned dining may be limited for some voyages.\xa0 \n 'Your Time Dining' Open Seating \n 'Your Time \xa0Dining ' is offered fleet wide.\xa0 Guests are seated on a first - come, first - served basis , depending on party \xa0size, and\xa0 in most cases, are accommodated within 20 minutes. Advance table reservations are not accepted .\xa0Guests using Carnival's HUB App can check-in for 'Your Time Dining' ahead of time or check-in when they are ready to go. The App will alert the guests when their table is ready and show the table\xa0number. All guests must be present in order for the party to be seated. The table\xa0will be held for 10 minutes.\xa0Your Time Dining is generally offered between 5:00pm and 9:00pm.*\xa0 \n Parties greater than 8 guests may need to be accommodated at several tables and the wait can sometimes be more than one hour.\xa0We highly suggest that parties of 8 or more guests choose an assigned seating to ensure sitting together at one table or several tables close together \n *Actual times will vary based on ship and itinerary, and will be listed in the daily ‘Fun Times’ and Carnival HUB App. \n At time of booking, guests will be able to confirm their preferred dining choice. If their preference is not available, they may confirm an alternate time and be waitlisted for their preferred choice ( there is no guarantee a waitlist will clear ) . When possible, waitlists will be cleared prior to the sailing and guests will be notified by email. T raveling parties who are waitlisted together will be cleared on the same dining time.\nCross-referencing bookings does\xa0 not \xa0guarantee parties will be seated together. They must be confirmed on the same dining time to ensure they will be able to dine together.\nFor those guests who choose e arly or l ate dining, the assigned dining room , time and table number , will be printed on the guests' Sail & Sign® card . \n Additional Dining Options\n In addition, guests may opt for casual bistro dining in the Lido Deck Restaurant or a more intimate and elegant atmosphere in the Steakhouse and other specialty dining venues. Please note, specialty dining options may have an additional charge. R estaurants and dining options vary by ship. Review dining options here .\xa0\xa0 \n NOTE:\xa0\xa0 Menu items (excluding Steakhouse Selections) are complimentary in the main dining room.\xa0 Guests can order a second entrée, keeping in mind they can also request half portions if something looks too enticing to pass up.\xa0 If a third entrée is ordered, a US$5 charge will be assessed."}, {'q': 'Does Carnival provide transportation from the airport to the cruise port terminal?', 'a': "Carnival Cruise Line offers\nground transportation between select airports and\xa0cruise ship terminals.\nThese services are only available on the day of the\xa0cruise and immediately\nafter the cruise.\xa0We do not offer airport transportation for cruises sailing from the following embarkation ports: Norfolk, Virginia: Baltimore, Maryland; Jacksonville, Florida; Mobile, Alabama; Charleston, South Carolina; Brisbane, Australia and Sydney, Australia. \n Purchasing\xa0transportation\ncan be done through Manage My Booking \xa0on\xa0 carnival.com \xa0or by\ncontacting Carnival Reservations up to\xa02 days prior to the sail date.\xa0 You will need to provide\nyour flight information in Online Check-in at the time of purchase. Your flight\ndetails are provided to the transportation company to assist in expediting your\ntransportation\xa0to the pier. \xa0It is your responsibility to update\nCarnival with any changes to your flight schedule to ensure you are met by the transportation\ncompany. \n Transfers can be purchased\nin\xa0four easy steps: \n > Log in to access My Cruise Manager \n > Click 'Shop' located at the top of the web page,\nthen select 'Airport Shuttle'. \n > Once on the 'Transfers' page, make your selection. \n > After you have made your transfer purchase, return\nto Online Check-In and provide flight itinerary. \n For the flight guidelines (latest airport arrivals and earliest\nreturn flights) and additional information\nabout\xa0airport\xa0transportation\xa0services, click here ."}, {'q': 'How do I get to my cruise port terminal?', 'a': 'BALTIMORE, MARYLAND\n Cruise Maryland Terminal at South Locust Point\n2001 East McComas Street\nBaltimore, MD 21230 \n Website: www.cruise.maryland.gov \n Parking: \xa0 www. cruise.maryland.gov/Pages/content/parking-rates.aspx \n Directions: \xa0 www.cruise.maryland.gov/Pages/content/directions-location.aspx \n Google Maps: \xa0 View Map \n GALVESTON, TEXAS\n Port of Galveston Cruise Ship Terminals\n2502 Harborside Drive\nGalveston, Texas 77550\n Website: \xa0 www.portofgalveston.com \n Parking:\xa0 \xa0 www.portofgalveston.com/91/Cruise-Parking--General-Information \n Directions:\xa0 \xa0 www.portofgalveston.com/90/From-the-North-West \n Google Maps: \xa0 \xa0 View Map \n JACKSONVILLE, FLORIDA\n Jaxport Cruise Terminal\n9810 August Drive\nJacksonville, FL 32226 \n Website: \xa0 www.jaxport.com \n Parking: \xa0 www.jaxportcruiseparking.com \n Directions: \xa0 www.jaxportcruiseparking.com-directions/ \n Google Maps:\xa0 View Map \n Note: \xa0Payment for parking can be made by credit card only .\xa0This includes payments at the parking lot entrance. P ay for parking online in advance at\xa0 www.jaxportcruiseparking.com \n LONG BEACH, CALIFORNIA\n Long Beach Cruise Terminal at the Queen Mary\n231 Windsor Way\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\nLong Beach, California 90802\xa0\xa0\n Google Maps: \xa0 View Map \n Note: Cruise terminal parking is limited. Off-site parking has been secured for certain sailings. Guests should review their emails communications to determine whether off-site parking is mandatory for their voyage, and consider the use of alternate transportation that does not require parking.\xa0 \n MIAMI, FLORIDA\n PortMiami \n1015 North America Way\nMiami, Florida 33132\n Cruise Terminal D - 1435 North Cruise Boulevard\nCruise Terminal E - 1265 North Cruise Boulevard\nCruise Terminal F - 1103 North Cruise Boulevard \n Website: \xa0 www.miamidade.gov/portmiami/parking-transportation.asp \n Parking: \xa0 www.miamidade.gov/portmiami/parking-information.asp \n Directions: \xa0 www.miamidade.gov/portmiami/directions-transportation.asp#directions \n Google Maps: \xa0 View Map \n MOBILE, ALABAMA\n Mobile Alabama Cruise Terminal\n201 South Water Street\nMobile, AL 36602 \n Website: \xa0 www.shipmobile.com \n Parking: \xa0 www.shipmobile.com/parking/ \n Directions: \xa0 www.shipmobile.com/directions/ \n Google Maps:\xa0 View Map \n NEW ORLEANS, LOUISIANA\n Port NOLA - Port of New Orleans\nErato Street Cruise\xa0Terminal\n1100 Port of New Orleans Place\nNew Orleans, Louisiana 70130 \n Website: \xa0 www.portnola.com \n Parking and Directions: \xa0 www.portnola.com/cruise/parking-directions \n Google Maps: \xa0 View Map \n NEW YORK CITY, NEW YORK \n New York Manhattan Cruise Terminal\n711 12th Avenue at 55th Street\nNew York City, New York 10019 \n Website: \xa0 www.nycruise.com/manhattan-terminal/ \n Parking: \xa0 www.nycruise.com/manhattan-terminal/parking/ \n Directions: \xa0 www.nycruise.com/manhattan-terminal/directions/ \n Google Maps: \xa0 View Map \n NORFOLK, VIRGINIA\n Port of Norfolk\nDecker Half Moone Cruise Center\nOne Waterside Drive\nNorfolk, Virginia 23510\n Website:\xa0 https://www.visitnorfolk.com/cruisenorfolk/#parking \n Google Maps:\xa0 View Map \n PORT CANAVERAL, FLORIDA\n Port Canaveral\nCape Canaveral, FL 32920 \n A-Side North Cruise Terminal #6 – 9241 Charles Rowland Drive \n B-Side South Cruise Terminal #3 – 220 Christopher Columbus Drive\n Website: \xa0 https://www.portcanaveral.com/Cruise/Port \n Parking and Directions: \xa0 http://www.portcanaveral.com/cruise/directions-parking/cruise-terminal-guide \n Google Maps: \xa0 View Map \n SAN FRANCISCO, CALIFORNIA\n Port of San Francisco\nThe Embarcadero \nPier 27 | Pier 35\nSan Francisco, CA 94111 \n Website: \xa0 www.sfport.com/ \n Parking: \xa0 \xa0 https://sfport.com/maritime/cruise#tab-12453-pane-2 \n Directions: \xa0 www.sfport.com/james-r-herman-cruise-terminal-pier-27-0 \n Google Maps: View Map \n SEATTLE, WASHINGTON\n Port of Seattle\nSmith Cove Cruise Terminal 91\n2001 West Garfield Street\nSeattle, WA 98119\n Website: \xa0 www.portseattle.org/places/smith-cove-cruise-terminal-pier-91 \n Parking: \xa0 www.cruiseseattleparking.com \n Google Maps:\xa0 View Map \n TAMPA, FLORIDA\n Port Tampa Bay\nTerminal #'}, {'q': 'What are Service Gratuities?', 'a': "It is customary for our guests to extend gratuities to the shipboard staff in appreciation for their hard work and exceptional service. 100% of your gratuities are distributed to the crew who you interact with, such as your stateroom attendants, dining and culinary services staff, as well as other members of the onboard team who work behind the scenes to enhance your overall cruise experience. Applying this charge automatically streamlines the recognition process and ensures our crew will share in your generosity.\xa0 \xa0\n To help you plan, we have provided the recommended onboard gratuities guidelines.\n Standard Staterooms: $17.00 USD per person, per day\n Suite Staterooms: $19.00 USD per person, per day\n You may pay this daily gratuity in two different ways:\n Pre-Pay \n Guests may call Carnival to\xa0purchase\xa0pre-paid gratuities\xa0at the time of booking up until sail date. If the final payment date of\xa0the cruise has passed, payment must be made at the time of adding the pre-paid gratuities. \n You may also add pre-paid gratuities on carnival.com at the time of booking or anytime up to 11:59pm ET, 2 days prior to sailing. \n If a guest booked with a travel agent, they may contact their travel professional to add pre-paid gratuities to their booking. Prepaid gratuities are reflected in the 'Miscellaneous Charge' field on the confirmation and in the guest's E-Documents.\xa0\n Sail & Sign ®\n If guests have not pre-paid their gratuities, the recommended, per person, amount will be posted to their Sail & Sign account during the cruise. Should a guest not be satisfied with the service they receive, they can contact the Guest Services desk while on board. This will allow us to address their concerns in a timely and appropriate fashion. At the discretion of the guest, gratuities may be adjusted after they have been posted on the guest's account, while on board. Gratuities, as posted on a guest's Sail & Sign account, will be considered final after a guest disembarks and no changes will be made after the cruise.\n Additional Information \n Gratuities are assessed on all guests, with the exception of children under the age of 2. \n Gratuities apply regardless of the dining options selected, such as eating at the casual dining restaurant or open seating dining. \n For beverage purchases, an 20% service charge will be added to the bill. \n A 20% service charge will be added to the reservation fee of all Specialty Dining venues as well as the nominal à la carte fee at Bonsai Sushi, Emeril’s Bistro, Guy’s Pig & Anchor Smokehouse | Brewhouse and Seafood Shack. Additional gratuities can be added at the guest's discretion.\n A 20% service charge will be added to the bill in the Main Dining Room for Steakhouse selections and Bonsai Sushi boat on dinner menu, Emeril's Bistro selections and fresh pressed juices on Seaday Brunch and breakfast menus.\xa0Additional gratuities can be added at the guest's discretion.\n A gratuity may be extended to room service staff as service is rendered. A 20% service charge will be added to the bill for beverages ordered from the bar through room service. \n Thank you for your generous recognition of our onboard team. Our crew works hard to provide you with a great vacation and takes pride in being part of the best team in the cruise industry."}, {'q': 'Can I get WiFi on board?', 'a': "To keep you connected while at sea, all ships provide satellite internet access from bow-to-stern.\n What kind of plans do you have? \n Social Wi-Fi Plan :\n This plan provides access to the most popular social websites and apps like Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp, Snapchat, TikTok, Pinterest, X, Reddit, LinkedIn, and major airline sites. \n It excludes access to most other websites, email, video, and music streaming services (e.g., Spotify, Netflix, Hulu), cellular-network-dependent Wi-Fi calling and FaceTime services. \n Pricing: *\nPre-cruise: $20.40 USD per day\nOnboard: $25.00 USD per day\n Value Wi-Fi Plan: \n Access all sites included in the Social plan with a faster connection speed. Ideal for travelers who want to stay in touch via social media, manage emails, browse, and stay updated on news, sports, and weather. \n It doesn't support video streaming or cellular-network-dependent Wi-Fi calling.\n Pricing: *\nPre-cruise: $23.80 USD per day\nOnboard: $32.00USD per day\n Premium Wi-Fi Plan: \n Experience superior internet performance. This plan offers access to all sites from the Social and Value Plans at speeds up to three times faster. You can stream movies, video chat, monitor your home and browse the web seamlessly, including apps like Netflix, Hulu, Spotify, FaceTime, Zoom, and Ring where coverage allows. \n Cellular-network-dependent Wi-Fi calling is not supported.\n Premium Multi-Device Wi-Fi Plan: Experience our fastest possible connection across up to 4 devices. This plan can only be purchased online prior to sailing for $90.00 USD per day and is not available onboard.\xa0The plan can be shared among guests in additional staterooms, not to exceed 4 devices.\xa0\n Pricing: *\nPre-cruise: $25.50 USD per day\nOnboard: $35.00 USD per day\n *Pricing is based on cruise-long plans and are subject to change without prior notice.\n Guests can upgrade from one plan to another and use multiple devices, per plan, including their smart phone or laptop, but only one device can be used at a time.\n How to purchase a plan? \n Pre-cruise: \xa0Pre-purchase internet plans at a discounted rate online via the 'Manage My Booking' tab on carnival.com or send as a gift to family and friends through The Fun Shops™. Guests must purchase a plan that covers the entire duration of their cruise. Plans may be pre-purchased online up to 11:59pm ET, the day before embarkation. Daily plans are available for purchase on board.\n On Board: \xa0Turn on your device's Wi-Fi feature and access the Wi-Fi settings to receive instructions on how to purchase our plans. \n What restrictions are there? \n Please note that as our services are carried via satellite, there are a few limitations compared to your home network.\n Sites blocked under the Carnival Fair Use Policy (adult content, violent content, etc.) will remain inaccessible under any plan or plan upgrade. \n All plans support for usage on one device at a time. \n Netflix and Hulu are supported, with individual subscriptions required. \n iMessage is included in all plans. \n FaceTime is available with both the Value and Premium plans. \n Satellite internet speed may vary depending on location and time of day. \n VPN connections are not supported. Discuss your VPN limitations with your company’s IT department if you are planning to work while sailing. We are not able to change your settings on board \n Pricing for plans purchased pre-cruise vary from plans purchased at time of sailing. \n There will be no refund after plan is activated on board. \n What are some tips to improve the experience? \n Once on board, turn on airplane mode and connect to Carnival Wi-Fi. By using airplane mode in settings, you avoid roaming fees charged by your carrier \n To benefit from faster speeds, turn off background app data services and updates \n Get the most from your cruise internet time and your trip — make sure you are powered up and prepared before you board the ship. Here are a few things you want to remember to pack for your cruise: \n Wi-Fi enabled laptop and"}, {'q': 'Does Carnival have a mobile app?', 'a': "To download the Carnival HUB™ App, look for the Carnival HUB App on Google Play and iTunes to download. You can also download the app from Carnival's website by clicking here . \n Which ships offer the Carnival HUB App?\xa0 \n All ships are Carnival HUB App capable. \n Where do the features of the app work? \n Some features are available before your cruise but more functionalities become available once on board. \n What does the Carnival HUB App do? \n The following features are available at the touch of your fingertips:\n Plan Ahead \n Share your cruise countdown \n Purchase gifts, WIFI, spa services, shore excursions and more \n Make dinner reservations \n Complete Online Check-In \n During Your Cruise \n Onboard Chat (fee applies) \n ‘What's Happening’ Daily Events \n Ship Maps \n Food and Drinks \n Account Management \n Kids and Teens \n Reserve select shows, spa services, shore excursions and specialty dining \n All your reservations are added to your planner to help you manage your day \n Reserve restaurants ahead of time or check-in if you’re ready to go \n View food and drink menus via QR scans \n Casino features and special events\xa0\n Lounging by the pool? Order food for delivery \n Learn about onboard safety and navigate to your assigned muster station to check-in with a team member upon boarding \n Check into a virtual queue and skip the line! We'll simply notify you when it's your turn \n And more... \n What is the app name? How can I download it? \n To download, look for the Carnival HUB App on Google Play and iTunes. You can also download the app from Carnival's website by clicking here . \n Is the Carnival HUB App free? \n The app is free to download and use on board. Starting at $5.00 USD per user, for the voyage, the HUB App offers chat.\n Do I need internet access to use the app? Do I have to pay roaming? \n No internet purchase is required. The app works only with the ship’s free Wi-Fi. To access sites and services outside of the HUB App, guests will need to purchase one of the Wi-Fi plans. To avoid carrier imposed roaming charges, turn on airplane mode while on board. \n How do I log into the Carnival HUB App? Where can I find my folio? \n You may log in before your cruise using your Carnival.com account or your booking details. To log on, once on board, you will need your folio number (found on your Sail & Sign card) and date of birth.\n Can minors use chat? \n Chat access is limited to ages 13 years and older. For safety reasons, parents and guardians must give consent within the app for guests 12 years and younger to activate onboard chat.\n What devices does the app work on? \n IOS/Apple iPhone versions supported: IOS 17 and up \n Android/Google versions supported: 11 and up \n Can I use my tablet to run the Carnival HUB App? \n Although the app is not optimized for tablets, it will function on both Android and Apple tablets."}, {'q': "What is Carnival's Tobacco and Marijuana Smoking Policy?", 'a': "Carnival Cruise Line is dedicated to the safety of all guests and crew. We want all our guests to have a safe, fun and memorable vacation. \n Smoking is a fire and safety hazard on a ship. Consequently, it is strictly limited to specific exterior deck areas.\xa0 All guests are expected to adhere to the following safety guidelines: \n All staterooms and suite accommodations, including outside balconies, are NON-SMOKING. This policy applies to all forms of smoking, including but not limited to cigarettes, cigars, pipes, vaporizers, electronic cigarettes and marijuana. \n Carnival recognizes that some state and local governments in the U.S., and in the destinations we visit, might allow marijuana use. However, Carnival Cruise Line follows U.S. federal law, which strictly prohibits possession and use of recreational/medicinal marijuana and other illegal controlled substances.\xa0 \n Any violation of this policy will result in a $500 charge, per violation, posted on the guest’s Sail & Sign® account and may also result in the disembarkation of all guests in the stateroom.\xa0 \n Guests who are disembarked for violating our policy will be responsible for all financial charges and expenses to return home, and no refund of their unused cruise fare will be provided. Additionally, they may be prohibited from sailing with Carnival Cruise Line in the future. \n Casino rules: There is no smoking in the casino unless seated and playing. It is not allowed at the casino bar or in the entire area when closed. \n Our smoking policy is included in Carnival's\xa0 Cruise Ticket Contract .\xa0 Follow the link for \xa0 ship specific smoking areas . \n In keeping with U.S. federal law, the minimum age to purchase tobacco products is 21. This policy is for U.S.-based itineraries/ships only. \n Frequently Asked Questions \n What happens if a guest is caught smoking in a stateroom or balcony? \n They will be assessed a $500 charge, per violation, on their Sail & Sign® account. Information on this charge is included in Section 8 of Carnival’s Cruise Ticket Contract. The assessment of this charge does not allow a guest to continue smoking in his/her stateroom. If a guest is found to be in violation of our smoking policy, all guests in the stateroom may be disembarked from the vessel and risk not being allowed to sail on Carnival in the future.\xa0 Guests will be responsible for all financial charges and expenses to return home, and no refund of unused cruise fare will be provided.\xa0 \n What should guests do if they smell tobacco in areas where smoking is not allowed, or marijuana in any area? \n Guests who are concerned about other guests violating our smoking policy should contact our onboard Guest Services team, so we can address the situation. This will help avoid uncomfortable situations between guests. \n Can guests bring marijuana/cannabis onboard for medical use? \n No. Marijuana is considered an illegal drug, and medical marijuana is not allowed onboard, during transfers to and from ships, inside terminals, during shore excursions, or when visiting private islands. Illegal drugs or substances will be confiscated, and appropriate action will be taken, which may include removal from the ship and involvement of law enforcement and other authorities. Additionally, foreign governments at ports of call enforce strict laws for drug possession. Guests found in violation of such laws are subject to arrest and prosecution by foreign authorities (and possibly the United States or other authorities) and may be prevented from re-boarding the ship.\n What if a guest has a letter from a doctor saying that they are allowed to use marijuana for medicinal and/or therapeutic purposes?\xa0 Why is that prohibited? \n Illegal narcotics/drugs including synthetic, designer drugs, marijuana, cannabis and cannabis derivatives such as Cannabidiol (CBD) items which may be labeled as medical marijuana are not allowed on board. While certain CBD products used for medicinal purposes may be legal in the U.S. based on sta"}, {'q': 'Can I bring bottled water on board?', 'a': 'Carnival’s\xa0 Liquor and Beverage Policy states that guests are prohibited from bringing water, sodas and other non-alcoholic beverages on board that are packaged in bottles.\n We know some of our guests are accustomed to bringing on board their own supply of bottled water, so for your convenience,\xa0bottled water can be pre-purchased prior to your cruise by visiting\xa0 www.carnival.com/funshops . \xa0Water will be delivered to your stateroom on embarkation day. Bottled water may also be purchased on board by contacting Room Service. Once on board, your purchase is non-refundable; you may take home any unopened bottles.\n $19.20 USD (includes 20% delivery fee) for a 12-pack of bottled water (16.9-ounce bottle/500-ml bottle)\n $5.40 USD (includes 20% delivery fee) for 1 large, bottled water (50.72-ounce bottle/1.5-liter bottle)\n $29.94 USD (includes 20% delivery fee) for 8-pack of bottled water (50.72-ounce bottle/1.5-liter bottle)\xa0\n Carnival carries distilled water for CPAP machines\xa0which can be purchased either pre-cruise or once on board. For pre-purchase, this can be purchased online at\xa0 www.carnival.com/in-room-food-beverages or by contacting our Fun Shops department at 800-522-7648, Monday through Friday, 9:00am-10:00pm ET and Saturday and Sunday, 9:00am-6:00pm ET. For purchase on board, please contact Room Service. Should you wish to bring your own distilled water with you, it must be hand carried along with your CPAP machine.'}, {'q': 'What items am I not allowed to bring?', 'a': "Carnival Cruise Line \n Prohibited Items, Exemptions, and Other Considerations \n Carnival Cruise Line prohibits weapons, illegal drugs, and certain items that could interfere with the safe operation of its ships or compromise the safety and security of guests and team members.\n Carnival conducts security screening of all luggage and reserves the right to confiscate any item that, in Carnival's sole discretion, is deemed dangerous or poses a risk to the vessel, its guests, or its team members. Confiscated items will be removed and disposed without compensation.\n To help avoid delays in the delivery of your luggage, we recommend leaving all luggage unlocked before turning it over to porters. For additional information, please refer to the terms and conditions of the Cruise Ticket Contract. \n Before you pack, please review the following information carefully.\n PROHIBITED ITEMS \n Illegal Drugs and Controlled Substances \n Illegal narcotics and drugs\n Synthetic drugs\n Designer drugs\n Marijuana and cannabis\n Cannabis-derived products, including Cannabidiol (CBD)\n Products labeled as medical marijuana\n While certain CBD products (for medical or other use) may be legal under some state or local laws within the United States, they remain prohibited under U.S. federal law and may also be prohibited in ports visited by Carnival ships.\n Weapons and Related Items \n All weapons and items designed, adapted, or intended to be used as offensive weapons are prohibited, including:\n Firearms and Projectile Weapons \n Firearms of any kind\n Replica or imitation firearms\n Firearm components\n Spears and spear guns\n Crossbows\n Crossbow bolts\n Longbows and arrows\n Paintball guns\n Air pistols and air rifles\n BB guns\n Pellet pistols and pellet rifles\n Blunt Weapons \n Brass knuckles\n Knuckle dusters\n Clubs\n Coshes\n Batons\n Flails\n Nunchaku\n Sharp Weapons \n Throwing stars\n Electronic Weapons \n Stun guns\n Tasers\n Chemical Weapons \n Gas guns\n Tear gas sprays\n Mace\n Phosphorus compounds\n Acids\n Other dangerous chemicals capable of incapacitating, maiming, or disabling a person\n Restraining Devices \n Handcuffs\n Any other restraint devices\n Ammunition \n Ammunition of any type\n Explosives and Flammable Materials \xa0\n Explosives\n Imitation explosives\n Explosive devices\n Fireworks\n Flares\n Pyrotechnics\n Flammable liquids\n Petrol (gasoline)\n Methylated spirits\n Paint thinners\n Hazardous chemicals\n Compressed Gases \xa0\n Compressed gas tanks\n Compressed gas bottles\n Compressed gas cylinders\n Dive tanks\n Propane tanks\n Aerosol cans\n Exception: Aerosol cans containing personal grooming products are permitted.\n Alcohol and Beverage Restrictions \n Alcoholic Beverages \n The following are prohibited:\n Hard liquor and spirits\n Beer\n Wine and Champagne \n Guests, 21 years or older, may bring on board one (1) 750 ml bottle of wine or champagne per person. \xa0\n Port wine\n Vermouth\n Sherry\n Any fortified wine exceeding 15% alcohol by volume (ABV)\n Non-Alcoholic Beverages \xa0\n Beverages in containers other than sealed cans or cartons\n Quantities exceeding 12 cans or cartons per person\n Containers are larger than 12 ounces each\n Electrical and Heating Devices \xa0\n Clothing irons\n Garment steamers\n Immersion heaters\n Heating blankets\n Water heaters\n Coffee makers\n Hot plates\n Toasters\n Humidifiers\n Electric heating pads\n For heat therapy, Carnival recommends either:\n Refillable heating pouches that use hot water, or\n Disposable heat therapy packs available at most pharmacies\n Sharp Objects \xa0\n Knives\n Scissors\n Open razors\xa0\n Recreational Dive Knives \n Allowed but must be checked with and maintained in the custody of vessel security\n May only be checked out for authorized dive excursions.\n Craft Scissors \n Large scissors used for scrapbooking or quilting may be permitted with prior approval from Security Services.\n Electronic, Communication, and Signal Equipment \xa0\n Emergency Position Indicating Radio Beacons (EPIRBs)\n Communication scanners\n Wideband receivers\n Satellite phones\n Transformers\n Las"}, {'q': 'How much luggage can I bring?', 'a': "To help you plan, we suggest you limit your luggage to a maximum of one bag per person, if traveling on cruises of 3-5 days duration, and no more than two bags per person, for cruises of 6 days or longer. In addition, you must personally carry-on any boarding documentation (passports, Visas, I.D), valuables, medications and items which require special handling.\n Guests who are scheduled to arrive at the terminal before 1:30 PM, usually check their bags with a porter so they can be free to enjoy lunch on Lido Deck before access to their stateroom is granted.\nChecked baggage service is only available until 2 hours before the ship's published sailing time (printed in the cruise documents).\xa0\xa0Guests arriving after this time will be responsible for taking their bags on board.\xa0\xa0\n Each checked suit case and carry-on suit case should not weigh more than 50 pounds, and when lying flat, bags must not exceed 16 inches high by 24 inches wide (the length of the bag is not a factor).\xa0For security screening purposes, all luggage should be unlocked. Oversized luggage and locked luggage may cause delivery delays.\xa0\xa0 \n Personalized luggage tags are included in the guest’s Electronic Documents (available once online check-in is completed). It is not necessary to print the tags in color. \n Carnival luggage tags must be affixed to your baggage prior to arriving at the terminal.\xa0\xa0Additional tags can be obtained at curbside from the porter. Porters will re-tag any luggage tag with a TBA cabin assignment.\xa0\xa0\xa0 \n Curbside porters are customarily provided a $1 tip per bag.\xa0\xa0They are not employees of Carnival and should a guest experiences any problems, they must report it to porter management on site. \n Since the screening and movement of large coolers through embarkation is an impediment to the boarding and security screening process, large coolers are not permitted as carry-on or checked luggage. Small, personal-sized coolers, no larger than 12 inches x 12 inches x 12 inches, for the purpose of housing small quantities of non-alcoholic beverages and/or medications are permitted as carry-on luggage. \nAirline Luggage Restrictions\n If traveling by air, guests are encouraged to contact the airlines directly to determine luggage restrictions and fees."}, {'q': 'What should I pack?', 'a': "To help you plan, on cruises of 3-5 days, please limit your luggage to a maximum of one bag, per person. On cruises of 6 days or longer, no more than two bags, per person. Each checked bag and carry-on bag should not weigh more than 50 pounds and, when lying flat, bags must not exceed 16 inches high, by 24 inches wide (the length of the bag is not a factor).\xa0For security screening purposes, all luggage should be unlocked. Oversized luggage and locked luggage may cause delivery delays.\xa0\xa0\n You must personally carry-on any boarding documentation (passports, visas, I.D), valuables, medications and items which require special handling or that you need access to while your checked luggage is being delivered. And don't forget your personal toiletries (travel size or standard container size). \n There are a number of must-pack items that we recommend every cruiser consider when preparing for a Carnival cruise. \xa0Before you get started, check out our What to Wear section and research the weather forecast for the ports you’ll be visiting to determine exactly what you will need to bring.\xa0 In addition, here are some other recommended items:\xa0 \n Collapsible daypack or bag\n Sunglasses\n Rain jacket or poncho and/or small umbrella\n Sunscreen and insect repellent\n Translation and guide books\n Books and magazines\n Binoculars (to see the beautiful wildlife in Alaska)\n Phone chargers\n Camera\n Checked baggage service is only available until 2 hours before the ship's published sailing time (printed in the cruise documents). Guests arriving after this time will be responsible for taking their own bags on board.\n What Not to Pack \n In order to maintain a safe and secure environment, Carnival prohibits certain items on board, such as weapons, candles, irons, alcohol, or other dangerous goods. Carnival conducts security safety scanning of all luggage and if prohibited items are found, they will be removed and disposed of and no compensation will be given. Please review our list of Prohibited Items before shutting your suitcase."}, {'q': 'What to wear?', 'a': "Cruisers love the fact they “only have to unpack once . ” And while your destination, itinerary and personal style will dictate which outfits you bring, we want to share our guidelines and suggestions. A Carnival ship has it all, from fine dining to casinos and shows to sunbathing, so here are some tips on how to dress to play or party. \n Daytime: Casual and Comfortable \n W hen the sun is up , c asual attire is the order of the day, which can include: \n Shorts, capris, khakis and jeans \n T-shirts, polo shirts, blouses and tops \n Summer dresses \n Exercise and athletic gear, lightweight sweater, pull-over or jacket \n Bathing suit, cover-up, hat or visor \n Comfortable rubber-sole flat shoes, sneakers, water shoes or non-slip boat shoes with traction \n \xa0 Please note : Select activities and shore excursions may require closed-toe shoes. Footwear with wheels is prohibited on board our ships. \n Evening: Cruise Casual \n As we head into the evening, the dress code\xa0 takes on \xa0multiple definitions, depending on your plans, the\xa0 venue \xa0or the event. \n Most nights, the dress code in the main dining room(s) for everyone is\xa0 “c ruise\xa0 c asual: ” \n Men and boys: sports slacks,\xa0 trousers,\xa0 khakis, jeans, tailored dress shorts and collared dress\xa0 shirts \xa0or button downs , polo shirts \xa0or nice\xa0 t -shirts \n Women and girls: casual dresses \xa0or\xa0 skirts, pants, capris, jeans,\xa0 blouses \xa0and\xa0 button down or pullover shirt. \n For voyages of 6 days or longer – and select shorter sailings (5 days or less) – pack your legwarmers, shoulder pads, and brightest neon attire for our '80s Rock-N-Glow Deck Party. And don't forget to bring an all-white outfit for the unforgettable White Hot Night Party, offered on 6+ day itineraries and select short-duration voyages (5 days or less). \n Not permitted: \xa0ripped/cut-off t-shirts, sheer, see-through and athletic clothing,\xa0 and \xa0swimwear \n Evening: Cruise Elegant (Sharp & Chic) \n On certain special nights, our main dining rooms celebrate our Cruise Elegant festivities , \xa0and we invite guests to enjoy a special night out in a sharp and chic way. \n Select 5 days or shorter cruises will have one Cruise Elegant evening (short duration voyages not hosting a Cruise Elegant evening will host a White Hot Night) \n 6 days or longer cruises will have two Cruise Elegant evenings \n On longer cruises, the first Cruise Elegant evening is scheduled for the second or third evening of the cruise. Depending on itinerary, the next Cruise Elegant evening is the second or third evening prior to the end of the cruise. \n Cruise Elegant \xa0(Sharp & Chic) \xa0attire can include: \n Men and boys: dress\xa0 jeans , \xa0trousers , \xa0slacks, dress shirts, and sport coats ( optional ); some men may even choose to wear a suit and tie or tuxedo \n Women and girls: dressy resort wear,\xa0 dresses (party or cocktail), pantsuits, elegant\xa0 skirts \xa0and blouses; some women may also wear evening gowns \n Not permitted:\xa0 r ipped/ c ut off\xa0 t -shirts, sheer or see-through clothing, athletic clothing or gear\xa0 and\xa0 swimwear \n A good rule of thumb is to dress for a special occasion. \n The Steakhouse and Rudi's\xa0 Seagrill dress requirements follow the dress code specified for the main dining room(s). \n The Lido Restaurant is open daily for breakfast, lunch and dinner and has a more relaxed dress code than the main dining room(s); however, please respect that the Lido Restaurant is not the pool area. Shirts, bathing\xa0 suit\xa0 cover-ups \xa0and footwear\xa0 must\xa0 always be\xa0 worn.\xa0 Please dry off completely as wet floors are a\xa0 safety \xa0hazard and always wear shoes/sandals, since open decks may become relatively hot. \n Casinos, bars, retail shops,\xa0 lounges \xa0and theaters are frequented by guests who dress according to daytime to nighttime standards. Basic rules still apply no matter the time of day – no swimsuits, wet clothes, or bare feet. \n Please Note : \n All guests are expected to ensure their clothing and accessories are respectful to fellow guests and reflect our family friendly atmosphere."}, {'q': 'Most Asked Questions', 'a': 'How do I enroll in Carnival Rewards? \n Log in to Carnival.com, or create or activate your account, and enroll in Carnival Rewards by accepting the program terms and conditions. Eligible Carnival Rewards Mastercard card members are already enrolled based on their credit card terms and conditions.\n How do I earn Carnival Rewards Points and Status Qualifying Stars? \n Members earn 3 Carnival Rewards Points and 3 Status Qualifying Stars for every $1 USD spent on eligible Carnival purchases. Points may be redeemed for eligible Carnival purchases, while Stars determine Carnival Rewards status. Other earning opportunities and exclusions may apply.\n When will my Points and Stars appear in my account? \n Points and Stars from eligible cruise fare, onboard spending, pre-cruise purchases, and casino play are credited to the member account approximately 14 days after the sailing is completed. During the 2026 transition, eligible pre-cruise activity may post separately at a later date. All earned Points and Stars will be captured and represented.\n How do I redeem Carnival Rewards Points? \n Eligible members may redeem Points toward cruise fare during booking or for eligible onboard purchases through the Carnival HUB app. Redemption for pre-cruise purchases will be introduced in a future release.\n How do I see my Carnival Rewards status and benefits? \n Your current Carnival Rewards status is shown in your profile on Carnival.com. Visit CarnivalRewards.com for information about the benefits available at each status level.\n How did previous VIFP Platinum and Diamond status carry into Carnival Rewards? \n Diamond: Guests who earned VIFP Diamond status by August 31, 2026, receive lifetime Carnival Rewards Diamond status after enrolling.\n Platinum: Guests who held VIFP Platinum status as of August 31, 2026, receive Platinum status through December 31, 2028 after enrolling. At the start of each new two-year earning cycle, they also receive a 10,000-Star boost, providing Gold status and a head start toward a higher tier.\n What if I was Platinum or Diamond but did not enroll before launch? \n To receive full Carnival Rewards status and benefits, eligible guests must enroll. Previous Platinum and Diamond guests must enroll before the end of 2028, subject to applicable data-retention policies, to receive the full transition treatment described above.'}, {'q': 'Getting Started with Carnival Rewards', 'a': 'When did Carnival Rewards begin? \n Carnival transitioned from the VIFP Club to Carnival Rewards on September 1, 2026.\n What happened to my VIFP number, and do I need to enroll? \n Your VIFP number automatically became your Carnival Guest Number. Every guest receives a Carnival Guest Number regardless of loyalty program participation. To fully participate in Carnival Rewards, eligible guests must enroll and accept the program terms and conditions in accordance with applicable law.\n Why did Carnival change the loyalty program? \n Carnival Rewards gives guests the opportunity to earn Points and Status Qualifying Stars based on eligible spending, plus the flexibility to redeem Points on the Carnival cruise experiences that matter to them.\n Where can I access my Carnival Rewards account? \n Log in to Carnival.com to access your Carnival Rewards account and view available account information.'}, {'q': 'September 2026 Transition Information', 'a': 'What if my cruise started before September 1, 2026, but ended on or after September 1, 2026? \n The following loyalty benefits apply to guest whose cruise began before the launch of Carnival Rewards and ends after the launch day:\n Manage Booking, Check-In, and the boarding pass remain under the VIFP experience for that sailing.\n The Carnival HUB app shows the guest’s VIFP benefits.\n VIFP benefits, days sailed, and milestone rewards are honored on the sailing.\n Carnival Rewards Points and Status Qualifying Stars are also earned for eligible activity throughout the cruise.\n Points, Stars, and milestone days from the sailing become available after the voyage returns.\n Why have Points and Stars from my eligible pre-cruise purchases not posted yet? \n During the transition period, Points and Stars from eligible pre-cruise purchases may post separately at a later date as system enhancements are completed. All earned Points and Stars will be captured and represented.\n What if I reached a higher VIFP status during a sailing that overlapped September 1, 2026? \n If you reached a higher VIFP status on a sailing that included September 1, 2026, Carnival will recognize the upgraded VIFP status as your Carnival Rewards status for the program transition period. You will also earn Carnival Rewards Points on eligible purchases tied to that sailing.'}, {'q': 'Earning Points and Status Qualifying Stars', 'a': 'What are Carnival Rewards Points and Status Qualifying Stars? \n Carnival Rewards Points are redeemable and may be used for eligible Carnival purchases.\n Status Qualifying Stars determine your Carnival Rewards status: Red, Gold, Platinum, or Diamond.\n Members earn 3 Points and 3 Stars for every $1 USD spent on eligible Carnival purchases.\n Members also earn 1 Point for every casino point remaining at the end of a sailing and 1 Star for every casino point earned.\n Carnival Rewards Mastercard cardmembers can earn additional Points and Stars under the card program.\n What spending is eligible to earn Points and Stars? \n Eligible categories include cruise fare, gratuities, transfers, Carnival Vacation Protection, and eligible pre-cruise and onboard purchases. Review the Carnival Rewards terms and conditions for the complete list of eligible categories.\n What spending does not earn Points and Stars? \n Excluded categories include Required Cruise Fees and Expenses, Government Taxes and Fees, air travel purchased through Carnival Fly2Fun, certain fare types, and other specified fees. Purchases made with Carnival Rewards Points, onboard credits, or Future Cruise Credits not originally funded by a guest’s own spending are also ineligible. Review the Carnival Rewards terms and conditions for the complete list.\n Do bookings and eligible pre-cruise purchases made before launch earn Points and Stars? \n Yes. Because Points and Stars are credited after a sailing is completed, eligible activity tied to a sailing ending on or after September 1, 2026, earns Carnival Rewards Points and Status Qualifying Stars. This includes eligible cruise fare, Carnival Vacation Protection, and other eligible pre-cruise purchases.\n How are Points and Stars from cruise fare divided among guests? \n Single occupancy: The eligible traveling member receives the Points and Stars related to the eligible cruise fare.\n Multiple eligible guests in one stateroom: Eligible cruise fare activity is divided equally among eligible guests in that stateroom.\n Minors: The responsible party receives the Points and Stars related to the minor’s portion of eligible cruise fare.\n Multiple staterooms: Eligible activity is allocated among eligible guests within each respective stateroom.\n Non-members: A non-member may enroll during the voyage or within 180 days after sailing to receive their portion. If they do not enroll, their portion is forfeited and is not reassigned.\n Purchaser not traveling: Points and Stars go to the eligible guests who travel, not to the person who paid for the booking.\n Who earns Points and Stars for onboard purchases? \n Eligible onboard purchases earn Points and Stars for the member whose individual folio is charged. They are also earned by members who use their Sail & Sign® card, including for purchases made through the Carnival HUB app. Purchases cannot be split between members after the fact. Members do not earn Points and Stars for onboard credit applied to a purchase.\xa0\n Will I earn Points and Stars on a booking made through a Travel Advisor or Personal Vacation Planner? \n Yes. Eligible bookings made through a Travel Advisor or Personal Vacation Planner earn Points and Stars. Exclusions may apply, including specified fare types and rate codes.\n Do I earn Points and Stars at Paradise Collection destinations? \n At Celebration Key and RelaxAway, Halfmoon Cay members earn 3 Points and 3 Stars per eligible $1 USD charged to their Sail & Sign® account.\n How do casino players earn Points and Stars? \n Casino activity is credited at the individual member folio level. Members earn 1 Carnival Rewards Point for every casino point remaining at the end of the sailing after any casino-point redemption for FunPlay, and 1 Status Qualifying Star for every casino point earned. Carnival Players Club benefits and offers are completely separate from Carnival Rewards.'}, {'q': 'Using Your Points', 'a': 'Where can I redeem Carnival Rewards Points? \nCarnival Rewards members can redeem points on:\xa0\n Cruise fare: Redeem Points during the booking process toward the deposit or eligible cruise fare. You may use a combination of cash and available Points.\n Onboard: Eligible members may redeem Points during the cruise through the Carnival HUB app for eligible onboard purchases, including shore excursions, specialty dining, spa treatments, drink packages, Wi-Fi, and more.\n Pre-cruise: Redemption for pre-cruise purchases is not yet available and will be introduced in a future release.\n Is there a minimum or maximum number of Points I can redeem? \n There is no minimum requirement to begin redeeming Points and no maximum redemption limit, provided you have enough available Points for the eligible purchase.\n What happens to unused onboard credit redeemed with Points? \n Onboard credit redeemed with Points is subject to the same eligible-purchase restrictions as regular onboard credit. Any unused portion at the end of the cruise automatically converts back to Carnival Rewards Points.\n Will onboard pricing be the same as pre-cruise pricing? \n Pre-cruise discounts are available only before sailing and may not be available onboard. Redemption of Points toward pre-cruise packages will be introduced at a later date.\n What happens to redeemed Points if a booking is canceled? \n Redeemed Points are refunded under the same rules as cash payments and are subject to applicable cancellation penalties.'}, {'q': 'Your Status and Benefits', 'a': 'What are the Carnival Rewards status levels? \n The status levels are Red, Gold, Platinum, and Diamond. Previous VIFP Blue tier guests who enrolled before launch transitioned to Red status.\n How do the Status Earning Window and Status Enjoyment Period work? \n The Status Earning Window is a fixed period that applies to enrolled members regardless of enrollment date.\n The first Status-Earning Window is September 1, 2026, through December 31, 2028. The next window is January 1, 2029, through December 31, 2030.\n If you earn enough Stars for a higher status during a window, your status is upgraded at that time. You enjoy the new status for the remainder of the current window and the following two-year Status Enjoyment Period.\n At the start of each new Status Earning Window, Status Qualifying Stars reset to zero and activity in the new window determines status for the following enjoyment period.\n How did previous VIFP Platinum and Diamond status carry into Carnival Rewards? \n Diamond: Guests who earned VIFP Diamond status by August 31, 2026, receive lifetime Carnival Rewards Diamond status after enrolling.\n Platinum: Guests who held VIFP Platinum status as of August 31, 2026, receive Platinum status through December 31, 2028 after enrolling. At the start of each new two-year earning cycle, they also receive a 10,000-Star boost, providing Gold status and a head start toward a higher tier.\n What if I was Platinum or Diamond but did not enroll before launch? \n To receive full Carnival Rewards status and benefits, eligible guests must enroll. Previous Platinum and Diamond guests must enroll before the end of 2028, subject to applicable data-retention policies, to receive the full transition treatment described above.'}, {'q': 'Milestones and Days Sailed', 'a': 'How do Carnival Rewards Milestones work, and do my previous sailed days count? \n Carnival Rewards Milestones are based on days sailed. Enrolled members are recognized on the cruise where they reach 50, 100, 200, and each subsequent 100 days sailed. Days accumulated before launch carry forward for enrolled members. Recognition begins with the next milestone reached after launch; prior milestones are not awarded retroactively.\n What recognition is included with a Carnival Rewards Milestone? \n Milestones are celebrated onboard and may include Carnival Rewards Points, exclusive onboard gifts, a commemorative Sail & Sign® card, and recognition from the shipboard team.\n Do I need to be a Carnival Rewards member to receive Milestone recognition? \n Yes. You must be enrolled in Carnival Rewards to receive Carnival Rewards Milestone recognition and benefits.\n What changed from the previous VIFP recognition program? \n Carnival Rewards continues the Platinum and Diamond ship-specific pin. The previous VIFP gift and Gold pin are no longer included. The Carnival Rewards Milestones program recognizes members based on days sailed rather than number of cruises.'}, {'q': 'Carnival Rewards Members', 'a': 'Do Carnival Rewards Points expire? \n Points do not expire if you have eligible qualifying activity within a three-year period. Qualifying activity includes earning or redeeming Points. Each qualifying activity extends the expiration date by three years. Points do not expire for Carnival Rewards Mastercard cardholders while the applicable cardholder rule remains in effect.\n What happens if I do not enroll, opt out, or later enroll again? \n If you have not enrolled, you may request eligible Points and Stars for activity within the prior six months after enrolling.\n If you opt out, your existing Point balance expires at midnight on the opt-out date and becomes zero.\n Points earned after opting out expire six months from their individual transaction dates and cannot be redeemed until you enroll again.\n If you enroll again before recently earned Points expire, those unexpired Points remain available.\n Can Carnival Rewards Points or accounts be transferred to another person? \n No. Carnival Rewards accounts, Points, and Stars are non-transferable. This includes transfers to family or household members and transfers following a member’s death or divorce.\n What happens if I enroll or opt out during a voyage? \n If you enroll during a voyage, the Sail & Sign® card and Carnival HUB app may not reflect membership until a subsequent voyage. If you are traveling on back-to-back cruises, the updated membership status will be reflected for the next voyage. If you opt out during a voyage, the existing membership status remains reflected for the rest of that sailing.'}, {'q': 'Families and Minors', 'a': 'Can minors participate in Carnival Rewards? \n No. Guests under age 18 cannot participate. Minors sail with the same status and benefits as the responsible paying adult. The responsible adult receives the Points and Stars from the minor’s eligible pre-cruise and onboard spending.\n What happens to a minor’s previous Platinum or Diamond status and days sailed? \n When a minor turns 18, they may activate their Carnival.com account using their Carnival Guest Number and enroll in Carnival Rewards. A minor who held VIFP Platinum or Diamond status as of August 31, 2026, will receive the applicable status recognition after enrolling. Cruise days accumulated as a minor also carry forward, and the member will be recognized at the next Carnival Rewards Milestone.'}, {'q': 'Carnival Rewards Mastercard', 'a': 'What happened to FunPoints and my previous Carnival Mastercard account? \n FunPoints automatically converted to Carnival Rewards Points and appeared in the linked Carnival Rewards account. There was no action required to transfer the balance. The converted Points do not expire under the applicable cardholder rules.\n How does the Carnival Rewards Mastercard earn Points and Stars? \n Earn up to 6x Points on eligible Carnival purchases: 3x through the card plus up to 3x through Carnival Rewards.\n Earn 2x Points at eligible restaurants and grocery stores.\n Earn 1x Points on other eligible purchases.\n Earn up to 4x Stars on eligible Carnival purchases: 1x through the card plus up to 3x through Carnival Rewards.\n Earn 1x Stars on other eligible card purchases.\n Are Carnival Rewards Mastercard card members automatically enrolled? \n Yes. Cardmembers are considered enrolled based on their credit card terms and conditions, so no additional enrollment action is required to receive applicable benefits.\n Can residents outside the United States apply for the Carnival co-branded credit card? \n No. The Carnival co-branded credit card is available only to U.S. residents. Carnival does not currently offer a co-branded credit card or partnership for Canada, Australia, or other countries outside the United States.\n We recognize that many guests outside the U.S., including those in Australia and Canada, are interested in a Carnival co-branded credit card. The current card program is offered through a U.S.-based issuing partner and is not available internationally at this time. While we do not have any updates to share today, we continue to evaluate opportunities for international markets and will communicate any future developments if they become available.\xa0 \n Do authorized users earn Points and Stars? \n No. Only the primary cardholder earns Points and Stars from Carnival Rewards Mastercard activity.\n Will my card number change? \n Applicable cardholders receive a newly designed card, but the account number remains the same. Continue using the current card until the new card arrives.\n What happens if a card member opts out and later enrolls again? \n The existing Point balance expires at midnight on the day of opt-out. New card-earned Points may continue to post but expire six months after posting unless the cardmember enrolls again before each expiration date.'}, {'q': 'Planning Your Visit and General Information', 'a': 'What should I bring with me to Celebration Key? \n Essentials include your Sail & Sign card, towel from your stateroom, sunscreen, photo ID, a credit card and some cash for purchases at smaller vendors for shopping. Consider water shoes, a hat, and a refillable water bottle. \n What payment types are accepted at the destination? \n We recommend bringing your Sail & Sign® card , credit card and some cash for food and beverage purchases as well as retail shopping .\xa0 \n Are there ATMs at the destination? \n Yes, there is an ATM.'}, {'q': 'Getting Around', 'a': 'How far is the walk from the ship to Paradise Plaza? \n About a 10-minute stroll down a shaded pier—roughly the length of two American-football fields. \n Are there complimentary trams around the destination if I don’t want to walk? \n Yes. Complimentary trams shuttle guests around the destination on a continuous, hop-on / hop-off loop (no reservations needed). Trams arrive every few minutes, but seats are first-come, first-served—so walking will often get you there faster if you’re able. Celebration Key is designed for easy walking, with most portals just a few shaded minutes apart. \n How long does it take to walk around Celebration Key? \n At a moderate walking pace, it would take approximately 5 minutes to walk between each portal.'}, {'q': 'Beach and Rentals', 'a': "Are the waterslides free? \n There is a nominal fee, and packages available, for unlimited access to the Suncastle's two racing slides. Unlimited rides are also included with Cabana and Supervilla reservations.\n Please note: Daybed bookings do not include slide access. \n What beach and water gear is available or allowed at Celebration Key?\n Guests can rent beach mats, snorkel gear, kayaks, paddleboards, pool floats, and noodles. Small personal floaties and personal snorkel gear are allowed. Oversized inflatables may be restricted depending on crowd levels. Guests can bring their own snorkel equipment. \n Are beach chairs, towels, and umbrellas available at Celebration Key? \n Absolutely! Beach chairs and umbrellas are complimentary and can be found throughout the destination. Beach towels should be brought from the ship. If you purchased Pearl Cove Beach Club access, beach towels will be provided. \n Are lockers available at Celebration Key? \n Yes, day lockers are available for rent throughout the destination. In addition, phone chargers (USB-A and USB-C) will be available inside guest lockers for convenient use. For those with Pearl Cove Beach access, complimentary lockers are available at the Beach Club. \n Lockers are located at each of the 8 public restrooms , with an additional bank of lockers at the Beach Club . Two sizes are available: \n Large lockers fit a small rolling suitcase or 2–3 full-size backpacks \n Medium lockers fit small purses, drawstring bags, or wet/dry bags \n Guests may access their locker as many times as needed throughout the day. The rental only ends—and payment is processed—when the guest actively ends their reservation. \n Are phone charging stations throughout the destination? \n Chargers (USB-A and USB-C) will be available inside guest lockers for convenient use and outlets are available in large cabanas and super villas."}, {'q': 'Family and Children', 'a': 'What is the swim diaper policy? \n Regular diapers are not permitted in any pool facilities. Swim diapers are required for non-potty-trained children in the splash pad and shallow areas of Starfish Lagoon. If needed, a limited supply of complimentary swim diapers will be available at Guest Services, Shorex kiosks and rental kiosks in Starfish Lagoon and available for sale in certain retail shops.'}, {'q': 'Food and Beverage', 'a': "What is Island Eats, and what meals are included at Celebration Key?\n With Island Eats™, each guest can enjoy one complimentary meal at select fast-casual venues or receive 40% off one entrée at full-service restaurants. Kids eat free at full-service restaurants from the kids' menu if they haven’t redeemed their Island Eats meal. Pearl Cove Beach Club is not included. \n Can I use my Cheers! onboard beverage package at Celebration Key? \n No. The Cheers! beverage package (and any other onboard drink packages) do not extend ashore. At Celebration Key, beverages are sold à la carte at the various bars. Only the Open Bar and the All-Inclusive Pearl Cove Beach Club package include beverages. \n Are there dedicated allergy-friendly dining locations? \n No, there are currently no designated allergy-friendly dining venues at Celebration Key. Please consult ship staff before disembarking for any specific dietary needs. \n Can I bring a cooler or outside food to Celebration Key? \n No, outside food and beverages are not permitted. A wide range of complimentary and for-purchase food options are available throughout the destination."}, {'q': 'Shopping and Services', 'a': 'Is there shopping on the island? \n Yes—stop by Lokono Cove for two great options: Shopper’s Paradise (local & duty-free goods) and the Straw & Artisan Market for handcrafted Bahamian items. \n Will purchases from local vendors at Celebration Key be delivered to the ship? \n No, guests are responsible for carrying any purchases back to the ship except for Duty Free items. Guests should plan accordingly for fragile or bulky items.'}, {'q': 'Experiences and Activities', 'a': 'What excursions are available at Celebration Key? \n Celebration Key offers a variety of exciting shore excursions for guests to enjoy. Guests can explore the available options and book excursions by visiting Carnival’s Shore Excursions page for Celebration Key. \n Are there height, weight, or age restrictions for any attractions at Celebration Key? \n Some slides, water activities, and shore excursions may have height, weight, or age restrictions. Please note the slides weight limit is 300 lbs., and the minimum height requirement is 40 inches. Details will be available in the Carnival Cruise Planner or at the Shore Excursions desk on board. \n What is Pearl Cove Beach Club? \n Pearl Cove Beach Club is Celebration Key’s exclusive, adults-only beach escape (18+), offering upgraded amenities such as infinity pool, luxury lounging, and premium food and drink options. Access is not included in your cruise fare and must be purchased separately. There are three beach club packages available – see the website for more details. \n Where can I reserve a daybed or cabana? \n You may reserve a daybed or cabana in advance through Carnival’s Cruise Planner. If spots remain, you can also reserve once on board via the Carnival HUB app, the Shore Excursions desk, or Guest Services—and, on the island, at Cabana Services kiosks or the concierge desk. \n Are there adult-only areas at Celebration Key? \n Yes. Pearl Cove Beach Club is the adults-only area with luxury amenities (additional fees apply). \n Is there any entertainment at Celebration Key? \n Absolutely! Celebration Key is filled with vibrant, family-friendly entertainment for all ages. Enjoy the colorful Junkanoo Rush parade, live Bahamian music, DJs spinning Bahamian vibes, and a variety of interactive activities and competitions. Weather permitting. For the latest times and updates, be sure to check the HUB App. \n Are there massage or spa services available at Celebration Key? \n Spa services are not currently offered at Celebration Key, but guests can enjoy a variety of peaceful beach and pool areas for relaxation. \n Can I have my wedding at Celebration Key? \n Weddings are not available currently but will be available in the future.'}, {'q': 'Connectivity and Technology', 'a': 'Is there Wi-Fi or high-speed internet access at Celebration Key? \n Yes! Guests with an active onboard internet plan can enjoy seamless complimentary Wi-Fi access at Celebration Key, just as they do onboard the ship. For those without a plan, 24-hour internet packages are available for purchase onboard the ship, not on destination. Even without an internet plan, the HUB App remains accessible, keeping you connected. \n Will my cell phone work at Celebration Key? \n Coverage varies by provider. Many guests will have roaming service in The Bahamas; check with your carrier for international roaming rates. Wi-Fi is available with a Carnival onboard plan.'}, {'q': 'Safety and Policies', 'a': 'Are there lifeguards at Celebration Key? \n Yes, Celebration Key has trained lifeguards stationed at pools and select beach areas for safety. However, guests should always supervise children in the water. \n Are there designated smoking areas at Celebration Key? \n Yes, cigarette, cigar, e-cigarette, vapes and pipe smoking are only permitted in designated smoking areas at Celebration Key. Guests can check wayfinding signs at the destination for specific locations. \n Are there any items not allowed at Celebration Key? \n Yes. For the safety and comfort of all guests, the following items are prohibited: \n • Glass containers \n • Drones (except in designated areas with prior approval) \n • Portable speakers \n • Alcohol brought from the ship \n • Grills or cooking equipment \n Are there life vests at Celebration Key?\n Life vests are available around the lagoon at Celebration Key, free of charge. There are no age requirements or restrictions as they are sized based on weight and chest measurements. There are currently three standard sizes available: \n Adult \xa0– 90 lbs / 41 kg, chest size 30–52 inches \n Youth \xa0– 50–90 lbs / 23–41 kg, chest size 24–29 inches \n Infant \xa0– 33–55 lbs'}, {'q': 'Accessibility and ADA', 'a': 'Are beach wheelchairs or strollers available? \n Beach wheelchairs are available free of charge on a first-come basis. Strollers are not available. \n Is Celebration Key accessible? What are the services for guests with disabilities ? \n We are committed to providing a relaxing and enjoyable experience for all our guests at Celebration Key. The destination includes a variety of accessible features to ensure a comfortable experience for guests with disabilities, including designated a ccessible trams available on regular rotation throughout the island. \n Are scooters allowed at Celebration Key? \n Yes. Guests are welcome to bring their scooters into port, and there are plenty of areas around the destination where they can park them. While there are electrical outlets throughout the island, please note that there are no designated scooter charging stations. \n Are there hearing or vision accessibility services available (e.g., assistive listening, accessible menus)? \n Not currently, but we recommend checking with the onboard guest services team for updates. All restroom facilities include accessible stalls. \n Is Celebration Key sensory inclusive? \n Yes. Celebration Key is officially certified as the first cruise destination to earn KultureCity’s Sensory Inclusive™ certification! More than 400 team members have been trained to support guests with sensory needs and invisible disabilities, helping ensure a welcoming and enjoyable experience throughout Celebration Key. \n KultureCity Sensory Bags are available for complimentary check‑out at Guest Services on Celebration Key, on a first‑come, first‑served basis, for the duration of your visit. These bags include noise‑reducing headphones, fidget tools, and strobe glasses designed to help reduce the impact of bright or strobe lighting. \n Can I bring my service animal to Celebration Key, and is there a relief area? \n Yes—certified service dogs may come ashore. Please notify Guest Services in advance; they’ll direct you to the island’s designated pet-relief area. Dogs must remain leashed at all times . Emotional-support animals are not permitted under cruise line policy and destination regulations.'}]